|||||||||Our story begins on a midnight walk... or in Gish and his tarball kids' case, a midnight roll. A roll rudely interrupted by a rancid little creature of the sewers...|Help!|Pfew! I know that stench... Hera's henchman from the Sewers of Dross!|Aw, don't you go worryin' about your little tarballs, Gish. We'll take gooood care a'them! Ahahaha! *cough*|Daddy! Help!|Shut yo' tarhole you little creep! Oh, Hera says hi. Hahaha! *cough* Smell ya later!|Hera? As in ex-girlfriend Hera? As in Hera who I threw into the lava Hera? And what does she want with my Eyelings anyway? This can only mean one thing... a sequel. Time to kick some ass and get to the bottom of this!|Gish becomes 'slick' when you change his surface by clicking the bottom left corner of the screen (his surface becomes brownish). When Gish is slick he can easily slide through narrow passages, but can't climb walls.|smazano|Buttons open doors and activate lifts. The light near the button is green if the lift/door is activated.|You found a secret passage! Find more to unlock bonus maps. There is at least one on every level so keep your eyes open!|Hey this is not how I designed the story! What's going on?! We're supposed to be in the sewers.|At least it doesn't smell that bad here...|About time someone built me a monumental statue. It looks adequately hungry and mean. Could be more round though...|Gish becomes 'sticky' when you change his surface by clicking the bottom left corner of the screen (his surface becomes grayish). When sticky, Gish can climb the walls and ceiling.||This wall is too slippery for Gish to climb.|Gish jumps best when he's flattened. Point up in the direction from Gish to jump. Keep the pointer there to jump higher. Stick to the top of the wall.|I feel the original plotline returning, Gish! Finally!|You know, I don't mind to kick Hera's ass in an alternative way.|Hm, that's strange, the water should be frozen at this temperature...|Dad! I chewed my way out of the sack and escaped!|Good boy! Don't forget to floss when you get home.|Aw, Dad!|Spikes and enemies can hurt you! You can see your health level in the top left corner of the screen. Raise it by collecting tarballs just like the ones next to you now.|Well lookee what we've got here. If it ain't our good ol' buddy Gish. I guess you was thinkin' you could just walk in here and see Hera? Hahaha! Hear that boys? Whaddya say we show our pal here how we look after guests?|Oh, is there complimentary ice cream?|Mr. Questionmark says, don't even try to kill the boss; explore the room instead.|Why do they keep doing this? The storyline has taken a different path again!|I guess it is because the only cool thing in your original story was me!|I... I will just quit this job, that's what I'll do.|You can also squish enemies by jumping on them when Gish is angry (click on his body).|And now for something completely different - Egypt! Don't ask me how we got here!|How did we get here?|I said...|Whatever.|This button must be kept down, otherwise the lift will stop. There is a box nearby, push it onto this button. You know the switch is activated when the light is green.|Another monument as a tribute to me! Aw, they shouldn't have...|Don't you think that it is a monument to somebody else? Perhaps to a bloodthirsty god of some tribal cultists?|Not really.|Why am I even asking.|Boxes can be easily operated if you stick them to your body and click on Gish to fire them away from you.|Well boys, it's a-lookin like our little tar buddy's come back for more. I ain't sittin' on no trapdoor this time! Now squish him, boys!|What's a matter? Too scared to fight me by your lonesome?|Bad news - I just got even more angry!|Hmm, something tells me this heavy box could help me get out of here. I just better not get in the way...|Well lookee who's got himself all trapped up! Poor little Gishy. Hope you're not claustrophobic! *evil laughter*|Psst! He doesn't know I just made a secret passage here!|Looks like I'm in for a slide... I knew I should've packed my snowboard!|You've gotta love the sound of squishing flesh, right? Right?!|You need to get this box to a button on the right side of the room. You can also throw it at an enemy to kill it (target the head). If the box gets destroyed, it will respawn at its original position. |Throwing the box up might seem hard, but after some practice it's a piece of cake.|So Hera really IS alive...|Ah, my darling Gish... don't look so surprised - do you really think lava would kill me? Ha! Lava can't harm you when you're as hot as I am! And now I'm going to be the most beautiful ball of tar ever! You'll never catch me!|Not catch you? Last I knew, you were slower than a legless drunk.|How dare you! We'll see who's legless here!|Um... actually we both are...|Shut Up! *starts to run*|Ha! Too slow you are, my Love. And now for the main course!|Bling bling!|Arg, Egypt. Probably loads of puzzles and traps just like last time. I hope you know what you're doing, thing which gets in my head and tells me what to do...|Um, I think Gish may be referring to *YOU* there.|*cough cough* Dad! This place, it's h-haunted! Run!|I ain't afraid of no ghost. |You haven't seen this one yet... *shudders*|A visitor! It's been... well, a while. Now I'm terribly sorry, but I suspect now that I must take your soul. It's a curse, you see. It's all in small print at the entrance to my tomb.|Uh huh. So, I see. And how were you thinking of doing that?|I shall cut you into small pieces with my super sharp sword, then catch your diminishing soul in the plastic bag I have with me.|How did my son put it? Ah yes... Ruuuuun!!!|Please! Anything but the light! Anything!|Anything, you say? *evil flash in his eyes*|Whatever you've got in mind, don't.|And on that day, Gish bravely defeated...|Piece of cake.|...the army of hideous cultists...|They are kinda cute in fact.|...who were threatening to enslave the whole world...|Just this island I guess.|Eergh! Would you please let me sound epic here!?|Oh, anytime!|So... we meet again. Do ignore my last performance; we all have our 'off days', don't you think? Now, there still is the pressing issue of me needing your soul. Unfortunately my tomb was built a few thousand years before central heating and it actually needs souls to be anything approaching comfortably warm.|Let me get this straight - you expect me to be your central heating?|No, Mr. Gish, I expect you to die.|Warmth! That's much better, thank you! Terribly sorry about the upset. All's well that ends well, I suppose. See you in the afterlife I'll wager!|Your alignment has been changed to 'CHAOTIC GOOD'|What the heck is chaotic good?|Oops, sorry, wrong game...|You know you don't have to kill everybody!|But I can! Ok I'll skip these two. Hope it'll make you proud.|You didn't think you could get rid of me so easily, Cutie, did you?|Actually, I did.|Well then you've got a lot to learn little boy. Look how little you are compared to me! And in 3 minutes I'll be even larger, after eating your kids!|Don't be so sure. What could you do to stop me?|Perhaps a double-reinforced door will do the trick? *evil laughter*|Mr. Questionmark points out that you can throw Hera by making Gish angry if he is stuck to her.|Now, where's my knife and fork?|Money money money; swinging is so funny, tra la la la la!|Hmm, strange smells, rats... let me guess, another sewer!|What the hell is that? It's got more teeth than a pool of sharks!|The god of the cultists! It's got tentacles coming out of the ground, too!|Aha! A weak spot! I will cut them off, one by one!|Who's your daddy?! You don't like this at all, do you!|You know you shouldn't kill this one. I like him.|Yeah he could be your boyfriend! I'll leave him but tell him to open this door for me.|Mr. Questionmark points out that you can break some springs. This one, for example.|We not hungry. We not kill you. We carry you over if you leave us alone. Grumpfl.|Just taking out the tentacles isn't going to work this time. Hmm, seems hungry... Wonder if he's ever tasted tarball?|As silly as it might sound, jumping into his maw is the only logical option.|Well, I hope I give you indigestion.|Hah! Looks like you bit off a bit more than you could chew!|Strike now, while the creature is doubled over in pain!|Now that was tough. Seems like they didn't like their god gone, haha! I feel we're getting back on the track with my story! Hurray for me!|Yeah. Whatever.|Hmm. Hera's skin sticks to me like chewing gum to the bottom of my shoe.|And now, you and I will stay here. Together. Forever! Forget about Brea! Think of the life we would share here!|Stay together? Here with you? After all that stuff about eating my kids?!|They are children of a human! Wake up, Gish! You can't be with a member of such a subrace! You are destined to be with me!|Well, in that case, it's time to kick destiny's ass!|Nooo! Then we must die together!|The walls of the cave are closing in to crush you!|*dramatic voice* and this is how our little drama ends...|Hang on, there's one more thing to do!|Ready! Aim! Fire!|Wait, wha- *kaboom*|Dad! You made it!|Sure I did! It's OK kids, you're safe now.|Er, yeah, about that...|?|It just didn't feel like a proper ending...|Alright, kids, what have you done?|Well, we kinda rigged the whole place to, well, explode.|You did WHAT?!|It's no good ending unless everything explodes, right Dad? We thought you'd be pleased.|We'll talk about this later, in the meantime.... Ruuuuun!!!|Welcome to my little playground. Feel free to play with the toys to the death. I'll be over here if you need me.|A long time ago in a sewer far away lived Gish and Hera. They were friends, close friends... lovers, actually. Like a Bonnie and Clyde of the tarball world, this infamous duo was well known for raiding tombs and sewers for trinkets and treasure.|Yeah!|Rock and roll!|If your teammate dies, you can revive him by collecting all his tarballs.|To complete a level, both of you must get to the level exit. Alive.|Ugh, what a stench!|Smells like...|...go on, say it, like the stuff which collects when a toilet leaks. Go on, everyone says it. You might as well too.|Actually, I think he's kind of cute!|*blushes* |Ok, that's it, we're going topside, Hera. And you'd better wash your hands or you're not getting any dinner.|Bye, sweet honey... bucket!|You think you have a chance in a squadron? Well you don't!|I should get my own piranha pets one day.|␀␀